# Verify UI in the browser harness

Cormux is a Tauri app. This agent session has no desktop/computer-use tools and no in-IDE browser MCP. Do not claim a UI change works after reading code.

After changing layout, styling, dialogs, routing, or click handlers:

1. Run `pnpm test:e2e` (starts Vite with the Tauri IPC stub in `src/lib/dev/browser-harness.ts`).
2. Read `e2e/output/new-workspace.png` (and any new screenshots you add) with the Read tool. Confirm the actual pixels, not just that the test passed.
3. If the flow is not covered, extend `e2e/` so it clicks the control and asserts visible outcome (dialog open, footer inside the card, no console pageerror).

`pnpm test` (Vitest) only covers pure TS helpers. It does not open the New workspace dialog.

Native macOS chrome (overlay traffic lights, dragging, Keychain) cannot be verified in Chromium. Say that explicitly. The user still has to run `pnpm tauri dev` for those.

If Cursor Browser MCP is enabled, also drive `http://127.0.0.1:1420` after `pnpm dev` — the same harness runs there (`html[data-cormux-harness=browser]`).
